  "requiredStatements": [
    "The prereg's cost estimate (about [US$ redacted] to 8.6 with the pilot) is above the [US$ redacted] trigger, so the cost rule was expected to cut the study to 2 control sequences. Sample used: 5-related; the control guard had 4 units and is therefore weak.",
    "Under the cost rule the sample was 5 related sequences, so 10 primary units: the primary holds only with 9 or more wins (9/10 gives one-sided p = 0.011; 8/10 gives p = 0.055); 8 to 2 is not an effect. Statement as preregistered: \"With 12 units the primary hypothesis holds only with 10 or more wins (10/12 gives one-sided p = 0.019; 9/12 gives p = 0.073): a 9 to 3 split is not an effect.\"",
    "Implementation choices fixed before the data, 2026-11-23: (a) a member's note-writing request lists at most the last 40 failing checks it saw during the case, the same in every arm, and the number left out is recorded per member; (b) the note-writing request after case 2 shows the member the case-1 notes of its arm in the same block as its other requests (notebook: its own notes; library: the lines about its module, cut at 300 tokens); (c) the cost rule compares the study's projection without the pilot with [US$ redacted] and also cuts back (2 control sequences, then 5 related) while that projection exceeds [US$ redacted] minus the pilot's actual spend, because the [US$ redacted] cap includes the pilot (no extra margin); the projection and the choice are written to results/gn1/plan.json with a timestamp before the first study wave; (d) the study cap against full reservations: each batch (part of a wave) reserves at most min([US$ redacted] [US$ redacted] minus committed), where committed is the spend so far with the pilot and unreconciled batches at their full reservation, down to a single request; when not even one request fits with nothing in flight, the study stops with a final exit and the numbers in results/gn1/cap-stop.json, so no unit is dropped silently.",
    "GN1-H5 (H-G27, no harm on fresh inputs): recorded inconclusive, read as \"not refuted (no harm detected)\"; it is never recorded as supported."
  ]
